# service_gap_placement_unmappable: A task's first placement list set over a read-only leaf, with SetObjectAndPlacementList (68). In the service the placement list must be mapped writable; that mapping fails and is left unmapped, and since there was no earlier placement list to copy, the command still succeeds. The next exec must map it and cannot ("Failed to map placement list"), so it faults, while a synchronize (53) of a buffer, which maps no list, completes. A second 68 moving the placement list to a writable page maps the old one read-only to copy from and succeeds, and the exec then runs. In-process, 68 is accepted (the device has the argument-buffer feature) but the task's list manager has no argument buffers: it records the object list and never the placement list, and every exec runs.
